course: dictionary
lesson: 12107
title: Coincide: same time, same idea, same place
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The verb coincide has three meanings, and context tells you which one you need. «My birthday coincides with the school holiday.» Here two things happen at the same time, so coincide means to happen together.
explain: «Our ideas coincide.» means our ideas are the same or agree. Ask yourself what fits: if two friends write the same answer, their thinking has met in the same place.
explain: In maths, shapes or lines that coincide lie exactly on top of each other. Fold a square in half: if the two edges match exactly, they coincide. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Coincide is a verb. Its forms are coincide, coincides, coincided and coinciding.
fact: Coincide can mean to happen at the same time, to agree or be the same, or to lie exactly on top of each other.
fact: The noun coincidence means a surprising thing that happens at the same time as something else, often by chance.
fact: With I, you, we and they, use coincide. With he, she and it, add an s: «It coincides.»
fact: The phrase coincide with is used when two things happen together: «The storm coincided with our picnic.»
exercise: «The school trip coincides with the football final.» What does coincides mean here? | Is cancelled | *Happens at the same time as, and agrees with | Happens at the same time as | Happens before
exercise: «Our answers coincide, so we both got 42.» What does coincide mean here? | Are different | Argue | Get lost | *Agree, or be the same
exercise: «The storm coincided with our picnic.» Find and copy the verb. | storm | *coincided | our | picnic
test: «When I fold the paper in half, the two edges coincide exactly.» What does coincide mean here? | *Lie exactly on top of each other | Go in opposite directions | Look blurry | Tear apart
test: «Meeting my cousin on the same train was a strange coincidence.» What is a coincidence? | *Two things happening together by chance | A type of train ticket | A very long journey | A rule everyone must follow
exam: «Our ideas ___ on almost every point.» Choose the correct verb form. | coincided | coinciding | *coincide | coincides
